message.content:
This looks like a CBP ruling on a child's Halloween costume of a pullover dress, socks and hat. Such costumes are generally classified as festive articles in 9505.90.6000 ("Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles: other"). However, textile costumes are often classified in chapter 61 or 62 if they are of a type that qualifies as wearing apparel. Since 2000s rulings, CBP treats costumes of flimsy construction as festive articles under 9505, as noted in Chapter 95 note 1(e), which excludes only "fancy dress of textiles, of chapters 61 and 62, being apparel of a kind worn..." Under the Note, costumes that are well made may be classified in 61/62. A Scarecrow costume made of flimsy material is typically 9505.90.6000.

The set includes a dress, socks and hat. The ruling probably held that the set is a festive article of 9505.90.6000, because of its flimsy construction and its use for Halloween.

